          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 19, 2019, at 12:30 AM, a witness decides to observe the sky from his balcony and take pictures with his smartphone. Between two photo takes, he notices the presence of three bright points arranged in a triangle. The witness sends GEIPAN photos and a video. Only one testimony is collected. The case consistency is good (one witness, photos, and a video of the observation). Analysis confirms the phenomenon's origin in the video as an optical reflection, leading to a GEIPAN classification as Category A: phenomenon explained by an optical reflection. However, the witness states he saw the phenomenon with his own eyes, which argument reduces the probability of the chosen hypothesis. The witness did not provide precise details about the PAN's positions in his questionnaire, referring only to the photos and video as descriptive elements. Thus, we only consider the analysis of the videos and photos (no astronomical analysis or other hypotheses). Therefore, GEIPAN classifies this case as Category B: probable misperception due to an optical reflection observed in the video.",
